+**Five roles, and `worker` no longer shares the application's.** `W-56` gave the worker
+`worker_user`, inheriting `app_user` rather than reusing its credential, so a mis-wired
+worker fails to connect instead of coming up healthy on the wrong secret. None of the five
+is superuser or `BYPASSRLS`; `DatabasePrivilegesIT` asserts the count and the matrix in both
+directions.
 
 **The application never connects as an owner.** That single constraint is what makes
 row-level security a real boundary rather than a suggestion — a bug in the application
